<div data-l="en"><section class="doc" id="guide"><h2>Course Guide: Digital Design with Verilog HDL 🎓</h2>
<p>This document describes the full content of the teaching module: <strong>42 supervised hours</strong> (+ 8 h of personal project work), intended for 2nd/3rd-year engineering-school or bachelor's students (electrical engineering, industrial computing, telecommunications, embedded systems).</p>
<p>All the tools used are <strong>100% free and open-source</strong>: <strong>Icarus Verilog</strong> (simulation), <strong>Yosys</strong> (synthesis), <strong>GTKWave</strong> (waveforms, optional).</p>
<hr />
