<h3>🚀 Quick Start (Ubuntu / Debian / WSL)</h3>
<pre><code class="language-bash">sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt install -y iverilog yosys gtkwave
cd pack_verilog
scripts/check_env.sh                           # checks the installation
scripts/run.sh 03_tp/TP1_combinatoire src      # tests YOUR code (src/ folder)
scripts/run.sh 03_tp/TP1_combinatoire corrige  # tests the solution
make help
</code></pre>
<p>Each testbench prints a last line <code>RESULT: PASS</code> or <code>RESULT: FAIL (n errors)</code>.
The script's exit code is 0 only on PASS: it can be used for automatic grading.</p>
<h3>📊 Built-in Visual Tools</h3>
<pre><code class="language-bash">scripts/wave.sh &lt;file.vcd&gt; tb.clk tb.q:dec --grid 10   # PNG/SVG timing diagram (no GTKWave needed)
scripts/show.sh &lt;module&gt; &lt;file.v&gt; [--gates]             # schematic of the circuit generated by Yosys (RTL or gates)
figures/make_all.sh                                     # regenerates all the figures of the pack (graphviz + matplotlib)
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> The figures are not drawn by hand. The timing diagrams come from real simulations, the schematics from <code>yosys show</code>, the measurement charts from Yosys (cells per module/type, cost of adders and of the ALU) and from a GCD latency model validated on 400 RTL simulations.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>👨‍🏫 Teacher's Guide</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Automatic validation:</strong> <code>make test</code> (or <code>scripts/test_all.sh</code>) checks that all the solutions pass, that all the student skeletons fail (non-trivial testbench) and that the FIFO mutant is detected.</li>
<li><strong>Validation result for this pack:</strong> "ALL CONSISTENT" (Icarus Verilog 12, Yosys 0.52+).</li>
<li><strong>Exam security:</strong> Do not distribute the <code>corrige/</code> and <code>mutant/</code> folders, nor <code>corriges_TD.md</code>, <code>corrige.md</code> and <code>pdf/*enseignant*</code> (teacher PDFs), before the end of the relevant sessions.</li>
<li><strong>Assessment:</strong> The 3 exams are independent and of comparable difficulty; the resit uses different modules from the final exam.</li>
<li><strong>GCD case study:</strong> The GCD of TP8 reuses the architecture (control/datapath, req/resp interface, 8 ports, 54 bits) of the supplied Yosys report; chapter C8 and TD4 use the figures from that report.</li>
</ul>
