<h3>Learning objectives</h3>
<p>By the end of the module, the student is able to:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Describe</strong> in Verilog (synthesisable subset) combinational circuits, sequential circuits and state machines;</li>
<li><strong>Structure</strong> a project hierarchically and in a parameterisable way (modules, <code>parameter</code>, <code>generate</code>);</li>
<li><strong>Verify</strong> a module with a self-checking <em>testbench</em>, using a reference model and random stimuli;</li>
<li><strong>Synthesise</strong> with Yosys, <strong>read a report</strong> (<code>stat</code>), and detect classic errors (latches, bus widths);</li>
<li><strong>Design</strong> a processing unit with a <em>control / datapath</em> split (GCD case study);</li>
<li><strong>Automate</strong> testing and synthesis with bash scripts and a <code>Makefile</code>.</li>
</ol>
