<h3>8.7 Key Points</h3>
<ol>
<li>Separating control and data makes the code <strong>readable, testable and reusable</strong>.</li>
<li>The val/rdy interface is a contract; the testbench must check it, not just the result.</li>
<li>We validate by simulation, then <strong>synthesise</strong>, read the report and <strong>re-simulate the netlist</strong>.</li>
