</ol></section><section class="doc" id="f2"><h2>F2 — PWM and LED "Breathing": Block Memory (BRAM) and ROM</h2>
<p><em>Duration: 3 h · Files: <code>src/pwm_rom.v</code> (to complete), <code>gamma.hex</code> (generated), <code>gen_gamma.py</code></em></p>
<h3>Objectives</h3>
<p>Modulate brightness with <strong>PWM</strong>; store a correction table in an inferred <strong>block memory</strong>; understand why
reading a BRAM is <strong>synchronous</strong>.</p>
<h3>1. Principle</h3>
<p>The human eye perceives intensity non-linearly: a linear ramp of duty cycle seems to "speed up" at low
values. We correct with a <strong>gamma</strong> table: <code>output = 255 × (input/255)^2.2</code>. The table is generated by <code>gen_gamma.py</code>:</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">cd F2_pwm_memoire_rom &amp;&amp; python3 gen_gamma.py &amp;&amp; cd ..       # writes gamma.hex (256 hexadecimal values)
</code></pre>
<h3>2. Work to Do (file <code>src/pwm_rom.v</code>)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong><code>gamma_rom</code></strong>: 256 × 8 ROM initialised with <code>$readmemh("gamma.hex", mem)</code>, <strong>synchronous read</strong> (inside an <code>always @(posedge clk)</code>).</li>
<li><strong><code>pwm8</code></strong>: free-running 8-bit counter; <strong>registered</strong> output equal to 1 when <code>cnt &lt; duty</code>; over 256 cycles the output is 1 exactly <code>duty</code> times.</li>
<li><strong><code>triangle8</code></strong>: on each <code>en</code> pulse, <code>val</code> rises from 0 to 255 then falls back to 0; 255 is reached only once per period (510 steps).</li>
</ol>
<p>The top-level module (supplied) makes two LEDs breathe: <code>LED[0]</code> <strong>with</strong> gamma, <code>LED[1]</code> <strong>without</strong>.</p>
<h3>3. Validate</h3>
<pre><code class="language-bash">scripts/fpga.sh sim F2_pwm_memoire_rom src
scripts/fpga.sh all F2_pwm_memoire_rom src     # requires 1 inferred SB_RAM40_4K block
scripts/fpga.sh prog F2_pwm_memoire_rom src
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Check on the board</strong>: [ ] LED[0] breathes without jerks, period 2 s [ ] LED[1] (linear) looks less smooth at low brightness.</p>
<h3>4. Questions</h3>
<ol>
<li>What is the PWM frequency? (12 MHz / 256.) Can the eye perceive it? Why is it suitable for an LED?</li>
<li>Why is the output <code>out</code> <strong>registered</strong>?</li>
<li>What becomes of the table if it is read with <code>assign q = mem[addr];</code>? Test the synthesis: how many <code>SB_RAM40_4K</code> blocks?
   (Observe and explain: the BRAM can only read at the clock edge.)</li>
<li>Replace 2.2 by 1.8 in <code>gen_gamma.py</code>, regenerate, run <code>fpga.sh all</code> again: what has changed (resource report, bitstream)?</li>
